>> title: Cachete, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, cheek, mexican, braise, tacos, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: cachete
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: cachete, cabeza, taco de cabeza, tacos de cachete, beef cheek, barbacoa de cachete, instant pot beef cheeks, pressure cooker beef cheeks
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-verde
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 40 min
>> slack: forgiving — the silverskin has to come off before it goes in, because nothing in the pot will render it down
>> step.2: trim the silverskin, season
>> step.3: brown 10 min, in two batches
>> step.4: 45 min high pressure, natural release 15 min
>> step.5: shred coarse, salt

The oven version has the cheeks half submerged and lets the rest cook off. Here one cup is the floor the pot needs to seal at all, and every drop of it is still there at the end.

Season @beef cheeks{3%lb}(1.4 kg; trimmed of the tough silverskin) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @coarse black pepper{1%tsp}.

Brown @&(~1)seasoned cheeks{} in @lard{1%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~brown{10%min}, in two batches, until each face is properly dark.

Pressure cook @&(~1)browned cheeks{} with @white onion{1}(quartered), @garlic{6%cloves}, @bay leaves{2}, @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, @whole cloves{3}, @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @water{1%cup}(240 mL), lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{12%min}, then ~pressure cook{45%min} on high and ~natural release{15%min}.

Shred @&(~1)braised cheeks{} coarsely with two forks, moistening them with their own liquor, and salt with @kosher salt{1%tsp}.
